# M-006 — Living Engineering OS Release 2

**Status:** Planned  
**Target gate:** 2027-02-14 (forecast)  
**Increment:** PI-EXP-003  
**Product Goal:** PG-004

## Outcome

Monad can operate across local, air-gapped, on-premises, and optional cloud profiles; clone/restore governed workspace state; reproduce environments; manage governed files/media; integrate through MCP/LSP/plugins/storage adapters; isolate optional external-runtime profiles; execute independent internal work deterministically in parallel; and meet declared scale/finalization benchmarks with complete security/provenance evidence.

## Acceptance

- WC-EXP-0010 through WC-EXP-0014 accepted;
- WP-EXP-0025 through WP-EXP-0040 closed or explicitly replanned without weakening PG-004;
- enterprise/offline and integration-surface conformance passes;
- plugin/storage/runtime adapters cannot redefine canonical semantic truth;
- parallel scheduling preserves deterministic result/evidence ordering;
- throughput/finalization claims include declared reference hardware/workload evidence;
- expanded security/scale/end-to-end journeys pass;
- migration from MVP Release 1 preserves canonical history and compatibility guarantees;
- PG-002, PG-003, and PG-004 receive explicit Product Authority acceptance or exact blocking evidence is recorded.

